WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:04.759
Venom and Spidey may very well meet on the
big screen again, but even with as much potential

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:09.290
as the clash could have, there are plenty
of reasons why Far From Home is far from the

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.440
right choice for another meeting between the
two.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.700
Here's a look at the reasons why it probably
won't happen.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:18.080
Venom's obviously much darker of a character
than Spider-Man.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.440
Eddie Brock wouldn't let his symbiote kill
cops in Venom, but when it came to crooks,

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.580
he had a more fluid moral compass.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:29.910
His solo film was PG-13 because the filmmakers
left a lot to the audience's imagination,

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:32.340
but make no mistake: He ate people.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.020
Heroes kill bad guys in Marvel movies, sure.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:39.430
Hawkeye's transformation into Ronin in Avengers:
Endgame was the darkest we've seen any of

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.560
their heroes go, but even then, no hero in
the MCU eats people.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:48.140
With Disney's acquisition of Fox, there are
likely a lot of conversations going on behind

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:49.560
the scenes about content.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:53.940
For example, we know Disney is interested
in more Deadpool movies and has pledged to

00:00:53.941 --> 00:00:58.559
not water him down for younger audiences,
but it's doubtful he'll be part of the larger

00:00:58.560 --> 00:00:59.860
MCU anytime soon.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:04.580
Likewise, it will probably be a bit before
Disney gives the thumbs up to superheroes

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:05.760
who eat muggers.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:09.810
One of the reasons Spider-Man and Venom's
conflict worked in the comics is that Parker

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:12.240
and Brock were in somewhat similar situations.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:16.500
They were roughly the same age, they were
both journalists working for New York area

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:20.939
newspapers, and, largely because of Brock's
competitive nature, they were rivals.

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.740
The movie situation isn't the same.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:26.640
In Venom, Eddie Brock is an established, adult,
investigative journalist.

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:29.020
Peter Parker hasn't graduated high school
yet.

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:34.380
Imagining the MCU’s version of Peter fighting
alongside someone like Venom is a little tough.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:38.380
In the trailer for Far from Home, he doesn't
even want to talk to Nick Fury on the phone.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:42.960
He's intimidated by Fury — so would he really
feel comfortable working with an oily pile

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.680
of black slime that talks like a gargling
demon?

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:46.380
Unlikely.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.900
"On my planet, I am kind of a loser.

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:49.660
Like you.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:51.640
But here, we could be more."

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:54.120
Spidey and Venom have met on screen before.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:58.240
Topher Grace starred as Eddie Brock in Spider-Man
3, and he wasn't alone.

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:01.679
His villainous character was joined by the
New Goblin and the Sandman.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:06.219
There were so many villains that Venom's eventual
appearance had to be held off until the end,

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:08.100
where it was rushed and unsatisfying.

00:02:08.569 --> 00:02:13.040
In Far from Home, we've already got Mysterio,
and possibly Hydro-Man, Molten Man and the

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:13.620
Chameleon.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:17.460
Not to mention all the rumors and theories
about secret bad guys.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:21.160
Most of them will be no-shows, but it's still
clear there's no room for Venom.

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:26.640
Tony Stark has been an obvious replacement
for MCU Peter's absent father, and even Adrian

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:29.340
Toomes acts as like a twisted parental figure
in Homecoming.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:33.400
From what we've seen of Far from Home, the
filmmakers have seemingly set up Nick Fury

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:36.120
and Mysterio as dueling mentor figures, too.

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:38.000
Fury offers tough love.

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:42.130
Since we know Mysterio is a villain in the
comics, he will probably be much friendlier

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:43.540
to gain Parker's trust.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:47.120
Throwing Venom in the mix would give us one
too many surrogate dads.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:52.180
Brock is, like most guys in this movie, older
than Parker, and has some abilities similar

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:52.680
to his.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.951
Once they stopped beating each other up, Peter
would see him as another role model, and he's

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:59.040
already got enough to deal with in that department.

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:04.620
As the Far From Home trailer indicates, the
MCU we know might just be one small part of

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:05.870
a wider multiverse.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:07.120
"Beck is from Earth.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.060
Just not ours."

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:13.100
If this is true, and the MCU is about to open
up in a similar way to what we saw in Spider-Man:

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:17.440
Into the Spider-Verse, then maybe Venom and
the upcoming Morbius take place in a kind

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:18.600
of parallel world.

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:23.120
If Spidey winds up traveling through the multiverse,
one of the places he visits could be the world

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:25.420
where Venom occasionally rides space shuttles.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:30.080
But there's also an alternate theory that
Mysterio is lying about being from another

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:34.100
Earth, and the multiverse has nothing to do
with what's going on in Far from Home.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:39.000
While Mysterio presents himself as an ally
of Spider-Man in the trailers and TV spots,

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:43.480
he's one of Spidey's oldest villains, with
abilities involving creating illusions to

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:44.260
trick people.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:48.900
It's totally conceivable he's not only tricking
Spider-Man, but Nick Fury as well.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:52.600
If that’s the case, then it would seem to
close the door on the theory that Venom might

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:54.300
show up because of the multiverse.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:59.070
The Venom movie not only divorced Eddie Brock's
story from Peter Parker's, it also established

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:03.340
itself as a force all on its own, inspiring
record-breaking ticket sales.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:07.920
All those profits helped Venom establish a
strong start for its franchise, with advance

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:11.890
ticket sales even outperforming a number of
successful MCU movies.

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:16.440
Basically, the character has become an entity
all his own, independent of Spider-Man.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:17.540
“You're welcome."

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:19.820
"No, YOU'RE welcome."

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:24.680
Introducing Venom to the crowded MCU now,
when he's just starting to make a name for

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:26.460
himself, could derail things.

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:31.080
His solo franchise would suffer if he's once
again seen as merely a Spidey spinoff.

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:35.380
Give Tom Hardy another movie or two with his
symbiote buddy, and then maybe he'll be ready

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:36.900
to co-star with Spider-Man.

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:41.260
Eddie Brock learns early in his most recent
comic series that his symbiote was on Earth

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:45.670
much earlier than he believed, and met a man
named Rex who had been merged with the alien

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:46.900
during the Vietnam War.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:52.080
Venom met and battled a space - named Knull
who held dominion over all symbiotes, and

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:54.520
learned Knull had fought Thor centuries before.

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:59.180
Since these revelations, Venom's origin has
taken on a more cosmic scope.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.500
If Marvel Studios wants to add Venom to its
movies, it may want to wait until it gets

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:07.400
the opportunity to introduce these newer,
grander aspects of his mythology.

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:09.660
There's already a lot going on in Far from
Home.

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:13.680
Knull, the All-Black, and everything else
would likely need their own movie separate

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:17.560
from Mysterio, multiverses, and Peter Parker's
newest crush.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:22.600
Disney has a deal with Sony, which holds the
movie rights to Spider-Man and related characters,

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:24.420
for Spider-Man to be in the MCU.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:26.620
That deal doesn't include Venom.

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:30.760
For the character to appear in a Marvel Studios
movie alongside Spider-Man, Sony would have

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:31.880
to agree to allow it.

00:05:32.389 --> 00:05:36.560
When Marvel and Sony hammered out their current
Spider-Man deal, Sony's attempts at rebooting

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:38.580
the Spider-Man film franchise had failed.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:42.080
They had a lot of motivation to work with
Marvel Studios.

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:44.600
That isn't necessarily the case with Venom.

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:47.280
In spite of being an utter disaster according
to critics…

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:52.430
"You are pathologically self-absorbed, your
ego requires constant attention, and you're

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:53.340
stubborn as hell."

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:55.200
...Venom made mountains of money.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:59.540
And while the character is strongly associated
with Spider-Man, he isn't so strongly tied

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:01.400
to the rest of the Marvel Universe.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:06.140
Arguably, as far as Sony's interests are concerned,
having Venom show up in Far from Home — or

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:10.200
any other Marvel Studios film — would serve
only to dilute the franchise.

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:11.840
So will we get more Venom?

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:12.460
Definitely.

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:14.480
Will he be teaming up with Spider-Man?

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:16.500
Probably not — at least, not yet.

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:19.540
"You gonna… you gonna eat anybody else?"

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:21.200
"Most likely."

